---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import PrimaryButton from "../components/buttons/PrimaryButton.astro";
import { readSettings, buildCanonicalUrl } from "../utils/settings";

const settings = readSettings();
const canonical = buildCanonicalUrl(settings, { path: "/about" });
const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "About" },
];
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="About WitchClick: secular ritual, tarot, and meaning-making for people building value outside the metric."
  canon={canonical}
>
  <Breadcrumbs slot="breadcrumbs" items={breadcrumbs} />
  <article class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none space-y-8">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <h1>About WitchClick</h1>
      <p>
        WitchClick exists for people whose real value is hard to measure from the outside: the sensitive, strange, grieving,
        nonlinear, creative, intuitive, slow-moving, pattern-noticing parts that do not always translate into a clean metric.
        This is a secular metaphysical space for making that value easier to feel and harder to abandon.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rituals and tarot here are reflective practices, not supernatural guarantees. We use symbols, cards, candles, lists,
        sensory anchors, and small repeated actions to choose a perspective on purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing here is medical, legal, or therapeutic advice. Take what helps, adapt every practice to your bodymind, and
        leave the rest at the door.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Brand manifesto</h2>
      <p>
        We believe magic is meaning-making with your hands in it. Not proof. Not prediction. Not a promise that the world will
        rearrange itself if you say the right words. Magic, here, is attention, perspective, symbolic action, and the choice to
        build a room where your inner life is treated as real.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Make space for worth that is not earned by output, polish, speed, or usefulness to someone else's plan.</li>
        <li>Treat ritual as a way to shift the lens, mark a threshold, and return to yourself with more honesty.</li>
        <li>Keep tarot secular, archetypal, and reflective: cards are prompts, not verdicts.</li>
        <li>Design for neurodivergent, disabled, and low-capacity readers as a baseline, not a niche feature.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Values we nurture</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Value outside the metric.</strong> You are allowed to matter before you are efficient, consistent, impressive,
          healed, monetized, or easy to explain.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reflective agency.</strong> Your autonomy matters more than any ritual. Every practice is an invitation to
          notice, choose, adapt, or stop.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Grounded wonder.</strong> Evidence, lived experience, folklore, intuition, and creative play can sit together
          without pretending to be the same thing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Accessible architecture.</strong> Low-spoons paths, plain-language notes, adjustable comfort settings, and
          short summaries are part of how the space is built.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transparent exchange.</strong> Affiliate disclosures, data practices, and pricing are plain to find. Money can
          support the work without becoming the measure of the work.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Boundaries we honor</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No spiritual supremacy.</strong> We do not appropriate closed practices or claim a single “correct” path to
          healing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No optimization bargain.</strong> WitchClick is not here to make you more palatable to systems that already
          misunderstand you. Growth can happen here, but self-erasure is not the price.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No purity tests.</strong> You can be skeptical, witchy-curious, or full-on occult nerd—everyone deserves tools
          that meet them where they are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No exploitation.</strong> Partnerships and recommendations must align with our ethics: fair labor, inclusive
          design, and joyful usefulness.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>If a collaboration or request crosses these lines, we decline clearly and keep the circle intact.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="membership" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Membership &amp; account roadmap</h2>
      <p>
        A dedicated member portal is on the horizon. It will hold bookmarking, saved reflections, ritual tracking, and printable
        libraries for readers who want their own saved corner of WitchClick. Until the infrastructure is ready, account
        links point you here so expectations stay clear.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to help shape the rollout? We are gathering testers who can share accessibility needs, pricing feedback, and the
        kinds of practices that would help you feel less translated through someone else's scoreboard.
      </p>
      <PrimaryButton href="/contact" iconAfter="↗">
        Tell us what you need
      </PrimaryButton>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
